  "title": "ICSI vs. conventional IVF: Which option is right for you?",
  "summary": "ICSI refers to a specialized form of IVF, in which a single live sperm is injected directly into the center of an egg, unlike in IVF, when thousands of sperm and one to two eggs are mixed in a single dish so the sperm can swim and penetrate the egg(s) just as they do during natural fertilization.",
